[Retroactive note added later, per the Symptom/Ruled out/Root cause/Fix commit-message framework]

Symptom: icon extraction from the .ico resource was relying on icotool's
automatic output-filename pattern (e.g. patcher_main_1_48x48x24.png).

Root cause: that auto-naming convention isn't a documented/guaranteed
contract — it's an implementation detail of icotool that isn't safe to
depend on across versions or builds.

Fix: use `icotool --index` with an explicit, controlled output filename
instead of guessing the auto-generated name.
